engine/science.md adapts the paper-review prompt of Liang et al., "Can large language
models provide useful feedback on research papers? A large-scale empirical analysis"
(arXiv:2310.01783), as distributed in Allen AI's marg-reviewer repository, and adds the
claims-to-experiments method of MARG (D'Arcy et al., "MARG: Multi-Agent Review Generation
for Scientific Papers", arXiv:2401.04259) and a condensed matter checklist.
engine/merge.md is original to this project.

engine/novelty.md's prior-work search follows the novelty check of Si et al.'s AI-Researcher
(https://github.com/NoviScl/AI-Researcher, MIT; no code used) and the facet comparison of the
Idea Novelty Checker (SDP 2025, https://aclanthology.org/2025.sdp-1.9; method only).

research/ holds the evaluation behind the plugin. research/eval/referee/*/referee.json and
the referee reports quoted in research/eval/ contain excerpts of published peer review files
from Nature, Nature Communications, Nature Physics and Communications Materials, and of
SciPost Physics reports. These are published under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Credit: Anonymous
Referee(s), in the peer review file of each article; each paper's arXiv ID, DOI and
peer-review source URL are listed in research/eval/referee/pool.json, papers.json and
candidates.json. The excerpts are shortened and summarized, which is a change from the original.

The AI reviews in research/ quote short passages from the arXiv preprints they review,
identified by arXiv ID, for the purpose of review and evaluation.

project-advisor/ adapts material from Anthropic's scientific-problem-selection skill
(https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins/tree/main/bio-research/skills/scientific-problem-selection),
by Anthropic, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The assumption analysis,
risk scale, red flags and fallback ("problem inversion") guidance in
project-advisor/skills/choose/references/assumptions.md are adapted from its references
02-risk-assessment.md and 07-problem-inversion.md, which follow Fischbach and Walsh, "Problem
choice and decision trees in science and engineering", Cell 2024. The adaptation shortens
them, replaces the biology examples with condensed matter and astronomy ones, and applies
them across several ideas at once.

project-advisor/skills/choose/references/prior-work.md describes a search loop modelled on
the novelty check in AI-Researcher (Si et al., https://github.com/NoviScl/AI-Researcher,
MIT License); no code is copied. Its facet comparison follows the method of the Idea
Novelty Checker (https://aclanthology.org/2025.sdp-1.9); no code is used.
